# A founding-file rule may only use a category already in the configured
# vocabulary (--category / the starter list): there is no --new-category at
# init — the vocabulary was chosen seconds earlier, so an unknown category is
# a typo, not growth. Could-not-run error (exit 2) naming the bad value and
# the vocabulary; nothing is seeded.

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-02

exitcode 2 constitution init --founding-file principles.md --category architecture --category process
stderr 'rule category "bogus" is not in the configured vocabulary \[architecture process\]'

# The refusal is atomic: no config, no log directory, nothing to clean
# up by hand (issues #22/#30). Before this, constitution.yml landed on
# disk carrying the trimmed vocabulary and every retry failed
# identically against it.
! exists constitution/adr/ADR-0001-founding-constitution.md
! exists constitution.yml
! exists constitution

# ...so re-running with a vocabulary that covers the rule just works.
exec constitution init --founding-file principles.md --category architecture --category process --category bogus
stdout 'init: constitution ready'
exists constitution/adr/ADR-0001-founding-constitution.md
grep '#### some-rule' constitution/adr/ADR-0001-founding-constitution.md

-- principles.md --
## Context and Problem Statement

x

## Considered Options

- a

## Decision Outcome

The body.

## Rules

### bogus

#### some-rule
Some rule text.
